    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "WHAT THIS DOES NOT SAY. It does not say \u2102 carries no order at all -- the lexicographic order on pairs is a perfectly good total order on Complex, and it satisfies le_refl, le_trans and add_le_add. It says no order is compatible with the RING structure, because sq_nonneg and zero_lt_one cannot both hold. Nor does it rule out CReal-valued statements about \u2102: Complex.normSq lands in CReal's existing nonneg cone (Complex.normSq_nonneg), which is available precisely because it is a statement about the components.",
        "type": "prose"
      },
